@startuml overview
' cumin-works - how a Maintainer opens a requirement issue together with Claude Code and the plugin.
' Render: run scripts/render-diagrams.sh at the root of the repository.

|Maintainer|
start
if () then (a new need)
  :tell the need;
else (an acceptance check left items\nthat need a decision)
endif
|Claude Code with the plugin|
:draft the requirement issue;
if (the repository has requirement documents\nand the need changes them?) then (yes)
  :draft the change\nof the documents;
else (no)
endif
:check the size, duplicates,\nblocked by, milestone, and assignee;
|Maintainer|
:agree;
|Claude Code with the plugin|
:open the pull request of the documents\nand the requirement issue;
|Maintainer|
:agree to start;
|Claude Code with the plugin|
:add cumin/status/ready;
stop

@enduml
